course: world
lesson: 124
title: Decades, centuries and millennia
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Big stretches of time have names: a decade is 10 years, a century 100 years and a millennium 1,000 years (two or more are millennia). "The eighties" means the decade from 1980 to 1989, not 80 years ago, and "the noughties" means 2000 to 2009.
explain: Centuries are counted from year 1, so the 1st century was years 1 to 100, and the century's number is one more than its hundreds: the 1800s are roughly the 19th century, and we live in the 21st, from 2001 to 2100. That's why a picky grandad says the new millennium really began in 2001, not at the huge parties of 2000.
explain: Lifetimes help you feel big times. A century is about 4 generations: you, your mum, your nan and your great-nan. Some people do live to 100, and Britain has about 15,000 of them. No person lives a millennium, though some bristlecone pine trees in the USA are over 4,000 years old.
explain: A century has about 36,525 days. The universe is about 13.8 billion years old, which is 13.8 million millennia, so huge that scientists measure it in millions and billions of years.
fact: A decade is 10 years, a century is 100 years and a millennium is 1,000 years.
fact: "The eighties" means the years 1980 to 1989, "the nineties" 1990 to 1999 and "the noughties" 2000 to 2009.
fact: The 1st century was years 1 to 100, so the 21st century runs from 2001 to 2100.
fact: The 19th century is 1801 to 1900, often called "the 1800s".
fact: The third millennium began on 1 January 2001, but most people celebrated in 2000.
fact: A person aged 100 or more is called a centenarian; Britain has about 15,000 of them.
fact: A generation is about 25 to 30 years, so 4 generations cover about a century.
fact: A century has about 36,524 or 36,525 days: 100 × 365 = 36,500, plus 24 or 25 leap days.
fact: No human lives a millennium, but some bristlecone pine trees in the USA are over 4,000 years old.
fact: The oldest people live about 120 years, so a millennium is about 8 of the longest lifetimes.
fact: The universe is about 13.8 billion years old, which is 13.8 million millennia.
exercise: How many years are in a decade? | 10 | 100 | 1,000 | 12
exercise: Grandma was a teenager "in the eighties". Which years does that mean? | 1980 to 1989 | 80 years ago | 1880 to 1889 | 1908 to 1918
exercise: How many years are in a century? | 100 | 10 | 1,000 | 50
exercise: Which years make up the 21st century? | 2001 to 2100 | 2100 to 2199 | 2000 to 2009 | 1901 to 2000
exercise: Which years are the 19th century? | 1801 to 1900 | 1901 to 2000 | 1900 to 1999 | 1701 to 1800
exercise: How many years are in a millennium? | 1,000 | 100 | 10,000 | 1,000,000
exercise: When did the third millennium really begin? | 1 January 2001 | New Year's Day 2000 | 31 December 1999 | New Year's Day 2100
exercise: What is a centenarian? | A person aged 100 or more | A Roman soldier in charge of 100 men | A person born in a new century | A coin that is worth 100 pennies
exercise: About how many centenarians live in Britain? | About 15,000 | About 15 | About 1,500,000 | About 150
exercise: About how long is one generation? | 25 to 30 years | 5 to 10 years | 100 years | 1,000 years
exercise: About how many generations fit in a century? | About 4 | About 10 | About 1 or 2 | About 40
exercise: About how many days are in a century? | About 36,525 | About 3,650 | About 365,000 | About 10,000
exercise: Can any living thing be over 1,000 years old? | Yes, some bristlecone pines are over 4,000 years old | No, nothing alive is over 100 years old | Yes, some people have lived 1,000 years | No, nothing alive is over 500 years old
exercise: Which years are the noughties? | 2000 to 2009 | 1900 to 1909 | 2010 to 2019 | 1990 to 1999
exercise: About how many millennia old is the universe? | About 13.8 million | About 13.8 | About 13.8 thousand | About 13.8 billion
test: Ruby: "Nan was a teen in the eighties? So, like, 80 years ago?" What's right? | The eighties are 1980 to 1989, about 40 years ago | Yes, exactly 80 years ago | It means when she was 80 years old | The eighties are 1880 to 1889
test: Tom: "21st century? It's 2026, not 2126, the teacher's well confused." What's true? | The 1st century was years 1 to 100, so the 2000s are the 21st | Tom's right, we're in the 20th century | The 21st century only starts in 2100 | Centuries are counted from the year 21
test: Freya, from Newcastle: "A millennium's a thousand years, like. Has any bairn been alive that long?" ("Bairn" means child.) What's true? | No person has, but some trees are over 4,000 years old | Yes, lots of people have lived 1,000 years | No living thing has lived over 200 years | Yes, but only people in ancient times
test: Grandad at a party in 2000: "Technically we're a year early, you numpties." Why? | Counting started at year 1, so the millennium began in 2001 | There was no year 2000 in the calendar | The millennium had begun back in 1999 | Grandad was looking at the wrong calendar
test: Kai: "100 years is ages, no one lives that long, no cap." ("No cap" means honestly.) Nan: "My nan did!" Who's right? | Nan: about 15,000 people in Britain are 100 or older | Kai: nobody has ever lived to 100 | Kai: only kings and queens live to 100 | Nan: nearly everyone lives to 100 now
test: Ella's family tree: her, her mum, her nan, her great-nan. About how many years might that cover? | About a century | About a single decade | About a millennium | About twenty years
test: Max: "How many days in a century, roughly?" Which sum gets close? | 100 × 365, plus about 25 leap days | 100 × 12, plus 24 | 100 × 52 | 10 × 365
test: Liam's teacher writes "19th century". His mate: "Easy, the 1900s, innit." Fix it. | It's the 1800s: take 1 from 19 to get the hundreds | He's right, it's the 1900s | It's the 2000s | It's the 1700s
test: Grace: "That song's from the noughties? It's like 20 years old, that's ancient, I'm dead." ("I'm dead" means I'm laughing so hard.) The song is from 2006. How old is it in 2026? | 20 years | 10 years | 60 years | 6 years
test: What would happen if centuries were counted from a year 0 instead of from year 1? | The 21st century would run from 2000 to 2099 | The 21st century would only run from 2100 to 2199 | There would be no 21st century at all, only the 20th | The 21st century would last a full 1,000 years
test: Ivy: "The universe is 13.8 billion years old? How many millennia is that, then?" | 13.8 million millennia | 13.8 billion millennia | 13.8 thousand millennia | 138 millennia
exam: Determine the span of years constituting the twenty-first century. | From 2001 to 2100 inclusive | From 2000 to 2099 inclusive | From 2100 to 2199 inclusive | From 1901 to 2000 inclusive
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the designation "the eighties", as employed in the phrase "a teenager in the eighties"? | The decade comprising the years 1980 to 1989 inclusive | A period commencing eighty years before the present | The century comprising the years 1800 to 1899 inclusive | The decade comprising the years 1880 to 1889 inclusive
exam: Ascertain the date upon which the third millennium commenced. | The first of January, 2001 | The first of January, 2000 | The thirty-first of December, 1999 | The first of January, 2100
exam: Given that a generation spans approximately twenty-five to thirty years, identify the approximate number of generations comprised in one century. | Four | Ten | One | Forty
